 "sq": [
  {
   "_id": 28964,
   "ANSWER": "<h2 data-end=\"136\" data-start=\"88\"><strong data-end=\"134\" data-start=\"91\">Features of ARM (Advanced RISC Machine)</strong></h2>\n\n<ol data-end=\"1643\" data-start=\"138\">\n\t<li data-end=\"289\" data-start=\"138\">\n\t<p data-end=\"164\" data-start=\"141\"><strong data-end=\"162\" data-start=\"141\">RISC Architecture</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"289\" data-start=\"168\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"224\" data-start=\"168\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"224\" data-start=\"170\">Uses a <strong data-end=\"214\" data-start=\"177\">Reduced Instruction Set Computing</strong> design.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"289\" data-start=\"228\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"289\" data-start=\"230\">Simple and uniform instructions lead to faster execution.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"454\" data-start=\"291\">\n\t<p data-end=\"323\" data-start=\"294\"><strong data-end=\"321\" data-start=\"294\">Load/Store Architecture</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"454\" data-start=\"327\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"390\" data-start=\"327\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"390\" data-start=\"329\">Only <strong data-end=\"342\" data-start=\"334\">load</strong> and <strong data-end=\"356\" data-start=\"347\">store</strong> instructions can access memory.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"454\" data-start=\"394\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"454\" data-start=\"396\">All other operations work on registers, improving speed.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"611\" data-start=\"456\">\n\t<p data-end=\"489\" data-start=\"459\"><strong data-end=\"487\" data-start=\"459\">Fixed Instruction Length</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"611\" data-start=\"493\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"542\" data-start=\"493\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"542\" data-start=\"495\">Most instructions are <strong data-end=\"527\" data-start=\"517\">32-bit</strong> (ARM state).</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"611\" data-start=\"546\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"611\" data-start=\"548\">Supports <strong data-end=\"573\" data-start=\"557\">16-bit THUMB</strong> instructions for compact code size.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"794\" data-start=\"613\">\n\t<p data-end=\"640\" data-start=\"616\"><strong data-end=\"638\" data-start=\"616\">Large Register Set</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"794\" data-start=\"644\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"700\" data-start=\"644\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"700\" data-start=\"646\">Typically <strong data-end=\"688\" data-start=\"656\">16 general-purpose registers</strong> (R0&ndash;R15).</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"794\" data-start=\"704\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"794\" data-start=\"706\">Includes <strong data-end=\"739\" data-start=\"715\">PC (Program Counter)</strong>, <strong data-end=\"763\" data-start=\"741\">LR (Link Register)</strong>, and <strong data-end=\"791\" data-start=\"769\">SP (Stack Pointer)</strong>.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"972\" data-start=\"796\">\n\t<p data-end=\"826\" data-start=\"799\"><strong data-end=\"824\" data-start=\"799\">Conditional Execution</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"972\" data-start=\"830\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"911\" data-start=\"830\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"911\" data-start=\"832\">Almost all instructions can be executed conditionally based on flag settings.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"972\" data-start=\"915\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"972\" data-start=\"917\">Reduces branch instructions and improves performance.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1123\" data-start=\"974\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1004\" data-start=\"977\"><strong data-end=\"1002\" data-start=\"977\">Pipeline Architecture</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1123\" data-start=\"1008\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1123\" data-start=\"1008\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1123\" data-start=\"1010\">ARM CPUs often use a <strong data-end=\"1059\" data-start=\"1031\">3-stage or more pipeline</strong> (Fetch, Decode, Execute) for parallel instruction processing.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1248\" data-start=\"1125\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1155\" data-start=\"1128\"><strong data-end=\"1153\" data-start=\"1128\">Low Power Consumption</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1248\" data-start=\"1159\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1248\" data-start=\"1159\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1248\" data-start=\"1161\">Designed for <strong data-end=\"1206\" data-start=\"1174\">energy-efficient performance</strong>, ideal for mobile and embedded systems.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1374\" data-start=\"1250\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1285\" data-start=\"1253\"><strong data-end=\"1283\" data-start=\"1253\">Orthogonal Instruction Set</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1374\" data-start=\"1289\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1374\" data-start=\"1289\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1374\" data-start=\"1291\">Most instructions can operate on any register and use different addressing modes.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1490\" data-start=\"1376\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1422\" data-start=\"1379\"><strong data-end=\"1420\" data-start=\"1379\">Support for Multiple Instruction Sets</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1490\" data-start=\"1426\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1490\" data-start=\"1426\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1490\" data-start=\"1428\">ARM (32-bit), THUMB (16-bit), and Thumb-2 (mixed 16/32-bit).</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1643\" data-start=\"1492\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1533\" data-start=\"1496\"><strong data-end=\"1531\" data-start=\"1496\">Enhanced Performance Extensions</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1643\" data-start=\"1538\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1596\" data-start=\"1538\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1596\" data-start=\"1540\"><strong data-end=\"1548\" data-start=\"1540\">NEON</strong> for SIMD processing (multimedia &amp; DSP tasks).</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1643\" data-start=\"1601\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1643\" data-start=\"1603\"><strong data-end=\"1610\" data-start=\"1603\">VFP</strong> for floating-point operations.</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ol>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2",
    "PLO14"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Discuss the features of ARM.&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 505,
   "TYPE": "sq",
   "key": 28964
  },
  {
   "_id": 28965,
   "ANSWER": "<h2 data-end=\"164\" data-start=\"118\"><strong data-end=\"164\" data-start=\"121\">R-Type Instruction Format (Register)</strong></h2>\n\n<ul data-end=\"265\" data-start=\"165\">\n\t<li data-end=\"215\" data-start=\"165\">\n\t<p data-end=\"215\" data-start=\"167\"><strong data-end=\"180\" data-start=\"167\">Used for:</strong> Register-to-register operations.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"265\" data-start=\"216\">\n\t<p data-end=\"265\" data-start=\"218\"><strong data-end=\"230\" data-start=\"218\">Example:</strong> <code data-end=\"247\" data-start=\"231\">ADD R1, R2, R3</code> (R1 = R2 + R3).</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p data-end=\"280\" data-start=\"267\"><strong data-end=\"278\" data-start=\"267\">Format:</strong></p>\n\n<pre data-end=\"384\" data-start=\"281\">\n\n&nbsp;</pre>\n\n<p><button aria-label=\"Copy\">Copy</button><button>Edit</button></p>\n\n<p><code>| Opcode (6 bits) | RS (5 bits) | RT (5 bits) | RD (5 bits) | Shamt (5 bits) | Funct (6 bits) | </code></p>\n\n<p data-end=\"406\" data-start=\"385\"><strong data-end=\"404\" data-start=\"385\">Field meanings:</strong></p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"717\" data-start=\"407\">\n\t<li data-end=\"448\" data-start=\"407\">\n\t<p data-end=\"448\" data-start=\"409\"><strong data-end=\"419\" data-start=\"409\">Opcode</strong> &ndash; Operation code (6 bits).</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"493\" data-start=\"449\">\n\t<p data-end=\"493\" data-start=\"451\"><strong data-end=\"457\" data-start=\"451\">RS</strong> &ndash; First source register (5 bits).</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"539\" data-start=\"494\">\n\t<p data-end=\"539\" data-start=\"496\"><strong data-end=\"502\" data-start=\"496\">RT</strong> &ndash; Second source register (5 bits).</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"583\" data-start=\"540\">\n\t<p data-end=\"583\" data-start=\"542\"><strong data-end=\"548\" data-start=\"542\">RD</strong> &ndash; Destination register (5 bits).</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"650\" data-start=\"584\">\n\t<p data-end=\"650\" data-start=\"586\"><strong data-end=\"595\" data-start=\"586\">Shamt</strong> &ndash; Shift amount (5 bits, used in shift instructions).</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"717\" data-start=\"651\">\n\t<p data-end=\"717\" data-start=\"653\"><strong data-end=\"662\" data-start=\"653\">Funct</strong> &ndash; Function code specifying exact operation (6 bits).</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr data-end=\"722\" data-start=\"719\" />\n<h2 data-end=\"771\" data-start=\"724\"><strong data-end=\"771\" data-start=\"727\">2. I-Type Instruction Format (Immediate)</strong></h2>\n\n<ul data-end=\"896\" data-start=\"772\">\n\t<li data-end=\"845\" data-start=\"772\">\n\t<p data-end=\"845\" data-start=\"774\"><strong data-end=\"787\" data-start=\"774\">Used for:</strong> Instructions with immediate values or memory addresses.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"896\" data-start=\"846\">\n\t<p data-end=\"896\" data-start=\"848\"><strong data-end=\"860\" data-start=\"848\">Example:</strong> <code data-end=\"878\" data-start=\"861\">ADDI R1, R2, 50</code> (R1 = R2 + 50).</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<p data-end=\"911\" data-start=\"898\"><strong data-end=\"909\" data-start=\"898\">Format:</strong></p>\n\n<pre data-end=\"989\" data-start=\"912\">\n\n&nbsp;</pre>\n\n<p>pgsql</p>\n\n<p><button aria-label=\"Copy\">Copy</button><button>Edit</button></p>\n\n<p><code>| Opcode (6 bits) | RS (5 bits) | RT (5 bits) | Immediate (16 bits) | </code></p>\n\n<p data-end=\"1011\" data-start=\"990\"><strong data-end=\"1009\" data-start=\"990\">Field meanings:</strong></p>\n\n<ul data-end=\"1191\" data-start=\"1012\">\n\t<li data-end=\"1053\" data-start=\"1012\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1053\" data-start=\"1014\"><strong data-end=\"1024\" data-start=\"1014\">Opcode</strong> &ndash; Operation code (6 bits).</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1092\" data-start=\"1054\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1092\" data-start=\"1056\"><strong data-end=\"1062\" data-start=\"1056\">RS</strong> &ndash; Source register (5 bits).</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1136\" data-start=\"1093\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1136\" data-start=\"1095\"><strong data-end=\"1101\" data-start=\"1095\">RT</strong> &ndash; Destination register (5 bits).</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1191\" data-start=\"1137\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1191\" data-start=\"1139\"><strong data-end=\"1152\" data-start=\"1139\">Immediate</strong> &ndash; 16-bit constant or address offset.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr data-end=\"1196\" data-start=\"1193\" />\n<h3 data-end=\"1224\" data-start=\"1198\">&nbsp;</h3>\n\n<pre data-end=\"1507\" data-start=\"1240\">\n\n&nbsp;</pre>\n\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "COURSE_CODE": "21CSS201T",
   "LEVEL": 2,
   "OUTCOMES": [
    "PLO1",
    "PLO2",
    "PLO14"
   ],
   "QUESTION_DESC": "<p>Draw the I-type and R-type register format in instruction encoding.&nbsp;</p>\n",
   "SESSION_ID": 505,
