 "lq": [
  {
   "_id": 37196,
   "ANSWER": "<p data-end=\"473\" data-start=\"219\">Computer systems can be classified based on <strong data-end=\"309\" data-start=\"277\">instruction and data streams</strong> using Flynn&rsquo;s taxonomy. This classification helps in understanding how multiple instructions and data are processed simultaneously. The four main categories are:</p>\n\n<hr data-end=\"478\" data-start=\"475\" />\n<h4 data-end=\"532\" data-start=\"480\">1. <strong data-end=\"530\" data-start=\"488\">SISD (Single Instruction, Single Data)</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"796\" data-start=\"533\">\n\t<li data-end=\"632\" data-start=\"533\">\n\t<p data-end=\"632\" data-start=\"535\"><strong data-end=\"550\" data-start=\"535\">Definition:</strong> A single processor executes one instruction at a time on a single data element.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"732\" data-start=\"633\">\n\t<p data-end=\"657\" data-start=\"635\"><strong data-end=\"655\" data-start=\"635\">Characteristics:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"732\" data-start=\"660\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"685\" data-start=\"660\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"685\" data-start=\"662\">Sequential processing</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"711\" data-start=\"688\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"711\" data-start=\"690\">Simple architecture</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"732\" data-start=\"714\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"732\" data-start=\"716\">No parallelism</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"796\" data-start=\"733\">\n\t<p data-end=\"796\" data-start=\"735\"><strong data-end=\"747\" data-start=\"735\">Example:</strong> Traditional personal computers, basic laptops.</p>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr data-end=\"801\" data-start=\"798\" />\n<h4 data-end=\"857\" data-start=\"803\">2. <strong data-end=\"855\" data-start=\"811\">SIMD (Single Instruction, Multiple Data)</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"1220\" data-start=\"858\">\n\t<li data-end=\"949\" data-start=\"858\">\n\t<p data-end=\"949\" data-start=\"860\"><strong data-end=\"875\" data-start=\"860\">Definition:</strong> A single instruction operates on multiple data elements simultaneously.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1072\" data-start=\"950\">\n\t<p data-end=\"974\" data-start=\"952\"><strong data-end=\"972\" data-start=\"952\">Characteristics:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1072\" data-start=\"977\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1016\" data-start=\"977\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1016\" data-start=\"979\">Exploits <strong data-end=\"1014\" data-start=\"988\">data-level parallelism</strong></p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1072\" data-start=\"1019\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1072\" data-start=\"1021\">Ideal for repetitive operations on large datasets</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1220\" data-start=\"1073\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1089\" data-start=\"1075\"><strong data-end=\"1087\" data-start=\"1075\">Example:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1220\" data-start=\"1092\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1167\" data-start=\"1092\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1167\" data-start=\"1094\">Graphics Processing Units (GPUs) used in image processing and rendering</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1220\" data-start=\"1170\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1220\" data-start=\"1172\">Vector processors used in scientific computing</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr data-end=\"1225\" data-start=\"1222\" />\n<h4 data-end=\"1281\" data-start=\"1227\">3. <strong data-end=\"1279\" data-start=\"1235\">MISD (Multiple Instruction, Single Data)</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"1580\" data-start=\"1282\">\n\t<li data-end=\"1371\" data-start=\"1282\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1371\" data-start=\"1284\"><strong data-end=\"1299\" data-start=\"1284\">Definition:</strong> Multiple instructions operate on the same data stream simultaneously.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1471\" data-start=\"1372\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1396\" data-start=\"1374\"><strong data-end=\"1394\" data-start=\"1374\">Characteristics:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1471\" data-start=\"1399\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1419\" data-start=\"1399\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1419\" data-start=\"1401\">Rare in practice</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1471\" data-start=\"1422\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1471\" data-start=\"1424\">Used for fault-tolerant systems or redundancy</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1580\" data-start=\"1472\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1488\" data-start=\"1474\"><strong data-end=\"1486\" data-start=\"1474\">Example:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1580\" data-start=\"1491\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1531\" data-start=\"1491\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1531\" data-start=\"1493\">Space shuttle flight control systems</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1580\" data-start=\"1534\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1580\" data-start=\"1536\">Some fault-tolerant multiprocessor systems</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr data-end=\"1585\" data-start=\"1582\" />\n<h4 data-end=\"1643\" data-start=\"1587\">4. <strong data-end=\"1641\" data-start=\"1595\">MIMD (Multiple Instruction, Multiple Data)</strong></h4>\n\n<ul data-end=\"2042\" data-start=\"1644\">\n\t<li data-end=\"1757\" data-start=\"1644\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1757\" data-start=\"1646\"><strong data-end=\"1661\" data-start=\"1646\">Definition:</strong> Multiple processors execute different instructions on different data elements simultaneously.</p>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"1891\" data-start=\"1758\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1782\" data-start=\"1760\"><strong data-end=\"1780\" data-start=\"1760\">Characteristics:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"1891\" data-start=\"1785\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1824\" data-start=\"1785\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1824\" data-start=\"1787\">Exploits <strong data-end=\"1822\" data-start=\"1796\">task-level parallelism</strong></p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1891\" data-start=\"1827\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1891\" data-start=\"1829\">Widely used in modern multiprocessor and distributed systems</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n\t<li data-end=\"2042\" data-start=\"1892\">\n\t<p data-end=\"1908\" data-start=\"1894\"><strong data-end=\"1906\" data-start=\"1894\">Example:</strong></p>\n\n\t<ul data-end=\"2042\" data-start=\"1911\">\n\t\t<li data-end=\"1959\" data-start=\"1911\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"1959\" data-start=\"1913\">Multicore processors in desktops and servers</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t\t<li data-end=\"2042\" data-start=\"1962\">\n\t\t<p data-end=\"2042\" data-start=\"1964\">Cluster computing systems for scientific simulations and big data processing</p>\n\t\t</li>\n\t</ul>\n\t</li>\n</ul>\n",
